[{:db/id 17592186110742 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-02b1f120-5924-58fd-afb2-36fdecec673f" "question-e3965a7d-c65e-545a-bf90-c696ecfb9f09"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110375 :question/worked-solution "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB = 3$ units\n\n- $CD=EF = 4$ units\n\n- $GH = 2$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent line segments is $\\overline{CD}\\cong\\overline{EF}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110741 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-76666e28-5611-55ce-b027-734929c0efa2" "question-d8399cd2-30cf-5b56-a133-fda3fd7126cd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110374 :question/problem "![](images/8b/8bc5a70179a245c26f766e7c0efb36b508d259746a6a92b02c4d423d39940d5a.png)\n\n  \n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AC=BD$\n\nII. $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$\n\nIII. $\\overline{AB}$ is congruent to $\\overline{BD}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that $AC= BD=5$ units.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $AB=CD=3$ units, we have that $\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{CD}$.\n\n- Statement III is false since $AB=3$, while $BD = 5.$ So, $\\overline{AB}\\ncong \\overline{BD}$.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110743 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-90696491-f11a-5ce4-ba23-2e9e528653c4" "question-bbeab3a9-f2b6-54a4-9522-21b49d07ec48" "question-51446c30-9b6a-505e-b4e5-79d8ad4dcdb4" "question-3f0cab83-1e6c-56a1-bd89-cee806fa30d5" "question-6bf86eb0-0d69-505c-9f67-1fb5751e701a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110376 :question/problem "For the diagram shown below, which of the following statements are true? \n\n![](images/79/793dacde520b1be4aa4a1e023760a06d1db5fe23266ec1277efe948e8ca04ab1.png)\n\n \n\nI. The segments $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BE}$\n\nIII. $BE = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. In the picture, both $\\overline{BC}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have the same double hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{BD}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, we can see that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BC}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BC} \\not\\cong \\overline{BE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the picture, we have that $\\overline{BE}$ and $\\overline{BD}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overline{BE} \\not\\cong \\overline{BD}.\n$$\n\nHence, ${BE} \\neq {BD},$ and since ${BD} = 4\\,\\textrm{cm}$, we have $BE \\neq 4\\,\\textrm{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-02b1f120-5924-58fd-afb2-36fdecec673f" :question/id #uuid "02b1f120-5924-58fd-afb2-36fdecec673f" :question/math-academy-id "q-52615" :question/problem "![](images/ed/ede04322d50034c955e6c954d99bfbfc1f13e7b7e40fd9eb12f660e995e018a0.png)\n\nWhich of the line segments shown above are congruent?" :question/worked-solution "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB=AC=4$ units\n\n- $DE=5$ units\n\n- $FG=6$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent segments is $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{AC}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c7b37f3-57d0-50b2-816e-291734505112"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c7b37f3-57d0-50b2-816e-291734505112" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7b37f3-57d0-50b2-816e-291734505112" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-fie